I guess this is a matter of taste, actually. I don't consider Mines' End
(or the Mines levels below Minetown) particularily difficult, and I
seldom die there (I die much more often in the similar depths of the
Dungeons). The only thing that really can go wrong in Mines is polytraps,
either a hostile monster stepping on one and turning into something nasty,
or the hero stepping on one and breaking out of the only dwarvish mithril
coat that has been found so far. If something providing MR has been found,
I would definitely go for the luckstone before descending too far into the
Dungeons - to identify it, if no other reason.

